Add a `column-anchor` layout option and per-output gravity.

Which edge new columns are anchored to, i.e. where the first column on a
workspace appears and which direction subsequent columns are added in:
`"left"` (current default), `"right"`, `"toward-center"`, or
`"away-from-center"`. The latter two are resolved per output against its
position in the connected-monitors layout (exposed as `gravity.{dx,dy}` on
`niri msg outputs`' logical output too), so multi-monitor setups can make new
columns grow outward from the seam between monitors instead of from a fixed
screen edge. `always-center-single-column` and `center-focused-column
"always"` keep taking precedence over the anchor.

Source: https://github.com/ppenguin/niri/tree/monitor-position-awareness-column-fill-direction
Regenerated against the niri-unstable rev pinned in this flake's lock so it
applies without fuzz; refresh it from that branch when it stops applying.
